# Point the frontend at the Python planning backend (server/). When set, the
# Run button sends every pane to POST $VITE_API_URL/plan instead of computing
# in the browser — every graph, the sample one included. Leave unset to run the
# built-in TypeScript planner, which has no Held-Karp and will say so.
#
# Spelled 127.0.0.1 rather than localhost on purpose: if any other service is
# listening on ::1, the browser resolves localhost there first and every plan
# request lands on it as a confusing 404 instead of reaching this backend.
VITE_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8787
